      },
      "text": "Breakfast at the hotel. An eight-hour tour with an English-speaking guide follows."
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:contentBlock_text:e9f37d752e8f327d",
      "field": "contentBlock.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "a2bb9c301e26feab845f8eaae36b80d58f13ddc7f3c838df4bf0636c7fbbe5f1",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-e2b3fa3e35a5",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      },
      "text": "On this full-day tour, visit the [replica of old El Peñol](/colombia/place/el-penol/), where the reconstructed town showcases a range of colonial architecture. Then head to the towering El Peñón, a 220-metre monolith.\n\nExplore Guatapé by motor taxi. The town is known for the decorative panels along the bases of its houses, where painted designs and raised reliefs brighten the façades. The final stop is at the El Peñol and Guatapé reservoirs, where green mountains rise above still, reflective water. Return to your hotel in the afternoon.\n\nDuration: eight hours."
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:media_alt:63bca8886e37d5d3",
      "field": "media.alt",
      "sourceTextSha256": "94770eaeea1d280b6c1601d30e3137944778a55847a6cd4a610ce40443165d8e",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-e2b3fa3e35a5",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      },
      "text": "Colonial square with a white church in the replica of old El Peñol, Colombia"
    },
